.TH "GYRO" "1" "Nov 2026" "Gyro Hosting" "gyro manual"

.SH NAME
gyro-server-agent-update - Update the guest agent


.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBgyro server agent update  [flags]\fP


.SH DESCRIPTION
Update the guest agent

.PP
Starts the automatic update through the old agent's fixed Gyro download channel (agent 3, or unknown version which is checked first); the server keeps running, about 30 s, then the private network settings are applied again. Refusals (409): \fBmanual_update_required\fR (agent 1-2: run \fBupdate_command\fR), \fBalready_latest\fR, \fBnot_running\fR, \fBnot_supported\fR, \fBbusy\fR\&. The task fails when the server cannot reach the internet; then run \fBupdate_command\fR from the web console. The Gyro guest agent configures private network cards and the public-IP-off route inside the server. Servers installed before 15 November 2026 run an older agent: a card attaches but \fBapplied\fR stays false and turning the public IP off answers 409 \fBagent_update_required\fR\&. \fBupdate_command\fR is a one-line command to run on the server as root (downloads Gyro's versioned updater and checks its SHA-256); it only replaces the agent, needs no restart and does not touch your data. If you gave the card an address yourself (netplan), delete that file and run \fBnetplan apply\fR afterwards.

.PP
API: POST /cloud/servers/{id}/agent/update (operationId updateServerAgent, scope cloud_write)


.SH OPTIONS
\fB--dry-run\fP[=false]
	show the price quote / request without changing anything

.PP
\fB-h\fP, \fB--help\fP[=false]
